---
title: Ordination of a Deacon: The Consecration
type: prayer
citation: BCP 544
bishop: true
bulletin: full
---

[Rubric] *All now stand except the ordinand, who kneels facing the Bishop. The hymn, Veni Creator Spiritus, or the hymn, Veni Sancte Spiritus, is sung. A period of silent prayer follows, the people still standing.*
[Rubric] *The Bishop then says this Prayer of Consecration*
[Bishop] O God, most merciful Father, we praise you for sending your Son Jesus Christ, who took on himself the form of a servant, and humbled himself, becoming obedient even to death on the cross. We praise you that you have highly exalted him, and made him Lord of all; and that, through him, we know that whoever would be great must be servant of all. We praise you for the many ministries in your Church, and for calling this your servant to the order of deacons.
[Rubric] *Here the Bishop lays hands upon the head of the ordinand, and prays*
[Bishop] Therefore, Father, through Jesus Christ your Son, give your Holy Spirit to *N.*; fill *him* with grace and power, and make
    *him* a deacon in your Church.
[Rubric] *The Bishop continues*
[Bishop] Make *him*, O Lord, modest and humble, strong and constant, to observe the discipline of Christ. Let *his* life and teaching so reflect your commandments, that through *him* many may come to know you and love you. As your Son came not to be served but to serve, may this deacon share in Christ's service, and come to the unending glory of him who, with you and the Holy Spirit, lives and reigns, one God, for ever and ever.
[Rubric] *The People in a loud voice respond*
[People] **Amen.**
[Rubric] *The new deacon is now vested according to the order of deacons. The Bishop then gives a Bible to the newly ordained, saying*
[Bishop] Receive this Bible as the sign of your authority to proclaim God's Word and to assist in the ministration of his holy Sacraments.

---

# The Peace

[Rubric] *The Bishop then says to the congregation*
[Bishop] The peace of the Lord be always with you.
[People] **And also with you.**
[Rubric] *The Bishop and the Clergy now greet the newly ordained. The new Deacon then exchanges greetings with family members and others, as may be convenient. The Clergy and People greet one another.*
